From a9cf19e16233865ffd4aa62d0f0a4d1549365b5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:37:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: coverage and lockstep guards, root validate,
 per-package CI legs

- verify:format-coverage and verify:typecheck-coverage ported from the
  Inspector, with the Inspector's tsc-program and resolve-node-bin libs
  (+ tests), adapted to npm workspaces via a new lib/workspaces.mjs that
  reads the root workspaces patterns from disk and checks the root
  validate still runs `npm run validate --workspaces`.
- verify:dep-lockstep: every shared toolchain devDependency (typescript,
  vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, prettier, @types/node) is declared with one
  range everywhere, or once at the root.
- Root validate = validate:guards (root format/lint, the guards,
  test:scripts) + npm run validate --workspaces.
- typescript.yml: each matrix leg runs only its own package's validate;
  the root-guards job runs validate:guards.
- Removes #4863's temporary verify:format-coverage wiring allowance, and
  fixes the four root-lint findings in the skills scripts.

Refs #4864

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
